hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2857","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Ubaid Ibn Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, that a captive came from Khawlan, and Aisha had a slave from the descendants of Ishmael, so a captive came from Yemen, So she wanted to be freed from them, “but the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade her.” Then a captive from Mudar came - I think he said: from the Banu Al-Anbar - “so he ordered her To be emancipated” followed by Shu’bah, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan
 [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 2857 - The hadith is authentic"
"2858","Ahmad bin Kamil bin Khalaf Al-Qadi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, and Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq told us, They said: Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Maqil, he said: Aisha had a freed slave. From the descendants of Ishmael, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought captive from the Banu Anbar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to her: “Emancipate “From the Banu al-Anbar, or from the Banu Lahyan, and do not free yourself from the Banu al-Khawlān.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
 Book of offices"
